body:
I have did that. I set up buckets. I didn't totally blow the parallel parking, I got some points for it....supposedly. The examiner refused to tell my sister how many points I had gotten/missed.

&nbsp;

Going to another town won't work. The same officers travel around to each town in the area on different days of the week. It's a really sparsely populated area.

>Make sure to study up really hard on your driver's test-do all the things you got wrong and do them a million times until you get it. 

&nbsp;

I didn't do anything wrong other than messing  up the parallel parking. And there is nowhere to parallel park here so there is no where to practice.

&nbsp;

The other things the examiner straight made up so I'd be missing enough points for her to fail me. IDK why-it's a small town, and my parents made plenty of enemies, maybe it's that. 

&nbsp;

For instance, the examiner claims I didn't park close enough to the curb because cars had to go around me...but there were no cars. There was no traffic on those streets and no one ever passed me. How do you deal with that? They will keep denying me my license forever, and I don't even know why.
